<Layout title="Research & accuracy" description="How StudentOffers handles research sources, missing information, verification dates, and offer statuses."><div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About', href: '/about/' },{ label: 'Research & accuracy' }]} /><header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Our approach</span><h1>Clear sources. Honest limits.</h1><p>Useful information includes knowing what still needs to be checked.</p></header><article class="prose"><h2>Where the information comes from</h2><p>The initial directory is based on three supplied research documents: Banking & Finance.odt, Mobile & Internet.odt, and Transportation.odt. Russian text has been translated into English, preserving documented prices, percentages, dates, and restrictions.</p><p>The banking document is dated 26 October 2026. The mobile document has no research date. The transport document is labeled 2026 without an exact date. Reviewing or importing a document does not establish when its research took place.</p><h2>What each status means</h2><ul><li><Status status="Active" /> — current availability and material terms have been independently confirmed.</li><li><Status status="Verification Required" /> — documented information is available, but current availability or some material conditions remain unconfirmed.</li><li><Status status="Expired" /> — a dated promotion or program has ended.</li><li><Status status="Archived" /> — a product is discontinued and retained for reference.</li></ul><p>A card and its promotion can have different statuses. For example, Amio’s five-year free-servicing promotion ended on 15 October 2026, while the standard card tariff is listed separately and requires current verification. VTB’s discontinued iStudent card is archived.</p><h2>Research is not independent verification</h2><p>Detail pages show the document research date, the date we reviewed the document for this site, and a separate independent verification date. An accessible website or a successful link check alone does not verify an offer.</p><p>Limited official-source checks on 26 October 2026 are described on the relevant detail pages. No listing has been marked Active solely because a provider page was reachable. Ucom’s retrieved postpaid call-network wording differs from the document; the discrepancy is shown on that plan’s page.</p><h2>Missing information stays visible</h2><p>We use “Not documented” or “Confirm with the provider” when the research does not establish a detail. No research in a category means no invented listings. A two-year benefit duration is not treated as an offer enrollment deadline.</p><h2>Banking and borrowing</h2><p>Free card servicing does not necessarily mean free transfers, cash withdrawals, or SMS. Cashback can depend on merchant category codes and monthly limits. Loans are listed as repayable financing, with missing rates, total costs, repayment periods, guarantees, and subsidy conditions explicitly identified.</p><h2>Check before you apply</h2><p>Offer conditions may change. Confirm current fees, eligibility, promotion dates, and required documents with the official provider. StudentOffers does not handle applications or student verification.</p><p>Found an error? Follow the <a href="/about/submit/">submission guidelines</a> to suggest a correction with an official source.</p></article></div></Layout>
